//   monster porting round (no src/kexgame/g_rogue_newai.ts exists yet).
//   Every `monsterinfo.blocked` handler in the base game calls
//   `blocked_checkplat` (not gunner-specific), so `gunner_blocked` genuinely
//   throws if a plat or a jumpable gap ever blocks this monster's path
//   today -- an honest gap, not a silent behavior change, mirroring
//   g_turret.ts's own `infantry_die`-family stub precedent for the identical
//   kind of missing-content-dir gap, AND matching the identical decision the
//   sibling m_gladiator.ts unit (landed in this same batch) already made for
//   this exact function/citation. `gunner_jump`/`gunner_jump2`/
//   `gunner_jump_now`/`gunner_jump2_now`/`gunner_jump_wait_land` are still
//   ported for real below (they're only unreachable via the stubbed
//   `blocked_checkjump` path today, not deleted -- a future g_rogue_newai.ts
//   unit can wire them back up with zero changes here).
// - NOTE ON WHAT IS *NOT* STUBBED: unlike `blocked_checkplat`/
//   `blocked_checkjump`, this file DOES locally port `PredictAim`,
//   `M_CalculatePitchToFire`, `M_MonsterDodge`, `monster_duck_down`,
//   `monster_duck_hold`, `monster_duck_up`, and `monster_done_dodge` for
//   real (see "PLACEMENT-MISMATCH FUNCTIONS PORTED LOCALLY" below) even
//   though every one of them is *also* only defined in
