// - `PredictAim`'s two C++ output pointer params (`vec3_t *aimdir, vec3_t
//   *aimpoint`, either may be `nullptr`) collapse to a single return value
//   `{ aimdir: Vec3; aimpoint: Vec3 }` -- `GunnerFire` (this file's only
//   call site) always wants `aimdir` and never passes `nullptr` for it in
//   the C++, so both are always computed and the caller just reads the
//   field it needs, mirroring `AngleVectors_destructured`'s established
//   idiom for the same "C out-params, TS destructured return" shape.
// - `M_CalculatePitchToFire`'s `vec3_t &aim` is an in/out reference
//   (mutated in place on success, left untouched on failure); ported as a
//   `Vec3` (mutable `Float32Array`) mutated via `vec3_copyInto`-style
//   in-place writes, not a return value -- the direct equivalent, matching
